  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-04-16T09:01:48.010Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "- Ability to use public and private proxies for all or some video links in VR Chat.\n\n  For example using an invidious instance proxy instead of connecting to Youtube directly in  a less private manner.\n\n- Toggles to allow automatic loading videos in some worlds and to disable video players in other worlds.\n\n  Using a VPN could mitigate a lot the issues with VR Chat I have listed above, but that's usually a lot slower and some VPN services block nonpaying customers from using peer-to-peer connections like Proton VPN which VR Chat is dependent on.\n\n  Unlikely to happen but desirable features:\n\n- Linux Support",
